DESCRIPTION:ACM International Conference on Future and Sustainable Energy S
 ystems (e-Energy 2027)\n\nRevision notification (winter deadline): 16 Apr 
 2027\, 23:59 UTC+12 (assumed)\n\nConference: June 5-11\, 2027\nLocation: A
 tlanta\, USA\nVenue: Hyatt Regency Atlanta\n\nAll dates:\n  Abstract regis
 tration (fall deadline): 11 Sept 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Paper submission (fal
 l deadline): 18 Sept 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Test of Time Award nomination sub
 mission: 15 Oct 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Author notification (fall deadline): 6
  Nov 2026\, 23:59 UTC+12 (assumed)\n  Revision submission (fall deadline):
  20 Nov 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Revision notification (fall deadline): 10 Dec 
 2026\, 23:59 UTC+12 (assumed)\n  Abstract registration (winter deadline): 
 8 Jan 2027\, 23:59 AoE\n  Paper submission (winter deadline): 15 Jan 2027\
 , 23:59 AoE\n  Author notification (winter deadline): 5 Mar 2027\, 23:59 U
 TC+12 (assumed)\n  Revision submission (winter deadline): 19 Mar 2027\, 23
 :59 AoE\n  Revision notification (winter deadline): 16 Apr 2027\, 23:59 UT
 C+12 (assumed)\n  Camera-ready due (both deadlines): 30 Apr 2027\, 23:59 A
 oE\n\nThe call for papers states no timezone. This is counted as UTC+12\, 
 the earliest it could plausibly mean\, so the countdown runs out before th
 e real deadline rather than after it.\n\n18th edition\, part of the inaugu
 ral ACM Sustainability Week and co-located with ACM FCRC 2027. Two submiss
 ion rounds\, fall and winter\; the fall round is recommended for authors f
 acing long visa processing. Each HotCRP site opens three weeks before its 
 deadline. Full papers are up to 10 pages and Notes papers up to 4 pages (9
 -point ACM sigconf\, double-column\, excluding references and appendices)\
 , double-blind. Full papers may be accepted\, rejected or asked to revise\
 ; the camera-ready version gets one extra page. Authors choose one of four
  tracks (Control and energy systems\, Learning\, Systems and applied model
 ing\, Theory). Selected rejected full papers may be invited as Notes paper
 s. Papers rejected in the fall round may not be resubmitted in the winter 
 round. Accepted papers from both rounds must be presented in June 2027. Pr
 oceedings are open access\; authors from institutions outside ACM Open pay
  a subsidised APC of $250 (ACM/SIG members) or $350. The ACM Digital Libra
 ry publication date\, which matters for patent filings\, may be up to two 
 weeks before the conference. Notification dates state no time or timezone.
 \n\nCall for papers: https://energy.acm.org/conferences/eenergy/2027/\nDet
 ails: https://powersystemdeadlines.org/preview/pr-11/conference/e-energy27
LOCATION:Atlanta\, USA
